# PART 7 — INTEGRATE PRIVATE SHARED CREATIONS WITH THE PUBLIC SHOWCASE

## 9. Connect Community Hub creator-showcase channels to public publishing

The existing private Community Hub already has creator-showcase sections.

These include:

- Games.
- Websites.
- Videos.
- Novels.
- All Shared Links.

Preserve the existing channel structure and interactions.

Do not redesign the chat interface.

### All Creations

The public All Creations section should aggregate approved, publicly published creations from the relevant categories.

It should not automatically display every private message.

### Individual categories

The public website should display approved items in the corresponding sections:

- Games.
- Websites.
- Videos.
- Novels.
- Experiments.
- Creative Tools.

The category structure should be configurable by the administrator.

Do not create a different hardcoded content source for every category.

Use a common content model with category metadata.

### Student sharing workflow

Students should have two ways to share their creations.

**Option A — Share through the private chat**

A student posts a game, website, repository or other creation inside the appropriate Community Hub channel.

That submission remains private by default.

The student may request that it be considered for public showcasing.

**Option B — Share directly through the public community**

An authenticated public user can create a public post or submit a creation through the Share Creation / Post button.

Apply the configured Review Mode rules before publishing.

The public publishing workflow must be separate from the private chat messaging workflow.

### Administrator curation workflow

Create or extend the administration tools so that the administrator can browse submissions and select creations for public showcasing.

The administrator should be able to:

- View the creator's original submission.
- View the original channel or submission source.
- Open the original game or website.
- View the provided description.
- Preview attached media.
- Select a public category.
- Edit the public display title.
- Improve or add a public description.
- Select or change the cover image, where permitted.
- Add appropriate tags.
- Approve the submission for public showcasing.
- Reject the request.
- Return it for additional information.
- Unpublish a previously published creation.

Do not modify the original private message when editing the public showcase details.

The public publication should retain a reference to its original source for administrative traceability.

### Student requests

Provide a clear way for a student to request public showcasing of a private creation.

The student should be able to see the request status:

- Pending review.
- Approved.
- Rejected.
- Additional information required.

Notify the student when an administrator makes a decision.

### Ownership and consent

Where a student submits a creation created by them, associate the publication with their account.

Before publishing a private-channel submission publicly, obtain explicit confirmation that the student is happy for the linked content and submitted material to be public.

Do not expose private names, school information or other sensitive student details without appropriate permission.

